 ## Subtopics
 
+### [Multi-resolution Surface Feature Encoding](12891-multi-resolution-surface-feature-encoding.md)
+Multi-resolution Surface Feature Encoding increases feature density in regions requiring high-frequency detail by creating virtual vertices within mesh faces, controlled by a per-face Level of Detail (LOD) factor $k_i$, without modifying the actual mesh topology. It addresses the limitation of sparse vertex distributions in neural global illumination, where insufficient geometric resolution hinders the representation of high-frequency illumination details. Unlike standard barycentric interpolation which uses only the three mesh vertices, this method subdivides each face into a regular triangular grid of virtual vertices, allowing for adaptive refinement based on training loss.
+
 ### Topology Sampling
-Topology Sampling assigns layers to faces by peeling the mesh from the outside in. It extracts the boundary, removes boundary tetrahedra, and repeats until all tetrahedra are peeled. Faces on the boundary at each step are assigned a new layer value. Boundary faces form layer 0; internal faces form subsequent layers [S1, unofficial].
+Topology Sampling assigns layers to faces by peeling the mesh from the outside in [S1, unofficial]. It extracts the boundary, removes boundary tetrahedra, and repeats until all tetrahedra are peeled [S1, unofficial]. Faces on the boundary at each step are assigned a new layer value [S1, unofficial]. Boundary faces form layer 0; internal faces form subsequent layers [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Step:** Initialize `CurrentLayer` to 0. Loop while there exists an unpeeled tetrahedron $t$. For each face $f$ in unpeeled tetrahedra, if $f$ is external, assign it `CurrentLayer`. Mark shared tetrahedra as peeled. Increment `CurrentLayer` [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Pitfall:** If all layer faces cannot be drawn because they exceed the internal face limit, a subset of layers is rendered by picking an even distribution of layers throughout the mesh until the target internal face count is reached [S1, unofficial].
